  <reporting-org ref="47045" secondary-reporter="0" type="30">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Global Fund to Fight AIDS, Tuberculosis and Malaria</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Towards Sustainable and Equitable Tuberculosis Control</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The program supported by this grant aims to reduce the burden of ill health due to TB in Malawi by pursuing high-quality DOTS expansion and enhancement; addressing infection control, MDR-TB and TB/HIV co-infection; engaging all care providers; and enabling and promoting operational research.  Grant funds will be used to mobilize communities to seek treatment; establish sputum collection centers in communities; provide high-burden laboratories in district hospitals with fluorescent microscopes; conduct a TB prevalence survey and an MDR-TB survey; and establish an electronic TB register in existing TB registration sites.  The program targets the general population, civil society, people living with HIV and AIDS; and TB patients and former TB patients.</narrative>
  </description>
